<title>SINGAPORE: Jaya Hldgs annual net profit up 12 pct.</title>
<headline>Jaya Hldgs annual net profit up 12 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    5.72   vs   5.09</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (cents)	4.10   vs   4.10</p>
<p>    EPS fully diluted (cents)	 3.90   vs   3.90</p>
<p>    Turnover			     86.73   vs  55.22</p>
<p>    Interest income		     2.58   vs   9.03</p>
<p>    Interest expense		    6.31   vs   4.45</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortization	19.12   vs  13.61</p>
<p>    Income from associates	    3.77   vs   2.50</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			7.76   vs   5.80</p>
<p>    Tax				     1.49   vs   0.44</p>
<p>    Minority interest		   0.55   vs   0.28</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		    2.50   vs   2.50</p>
<p>Books close: 3 December 1996</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: 12 December 1996</p>
<p>Note - Jaya Holdings Ltd, a shipping company, said the 57 percent turnover increase was attributable to its shipbuilding and conventional shipping divisions. The company said maritime trade was difficult in 1996 but that it expected the group result for this year to be satisfactory.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
